.TH git-harvest-assemble 1  "assemble " 
.SH NAME
git\-harvest\-assemble \- Merge the harvested fragments into a new CHANGELOG section
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-harvest assemble\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-changelog\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-input\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-released\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIVERSION\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Merge the harvested fragments into a new CHANGELOG section.
.PP
Reads every fragment file in the input directory, folds duplicate entries — the same change recorded by more than one fragment — into a single entry crediting every contributor who reported it, and writes the result as a new section for the given version. Every fragment consumed this way is then deleted; a fragment for a still\-unreleased change is left untouched.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-changelog\fR \fI<CHANGELOG>\fR [default: CHANGELOG.ron]
The CHANGELOG to merge the fragments into
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-input\fR \fI<INPUT>\fR [default: changelog.d]
The directory the fragments are read from and then cleared
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-released\fR \fI<RELEASED>\fR
The publish moment, RFC 3339; defaults to now, in UTC
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIVERSION\fR>
The version the new section documents, as `major.minor.patch`
